{
  "dom_id": "step-t2786",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "When solving an equation, we sometimes require taking the square root of a negative number. In such cases, we will not end up with real solutions, but imaginary solutions.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's solve the equation $2x^2 +8 = 0$ for $x.$ First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2x^2 + 8 &= 0 \\[3pt]\n\t\t2x^2 &= -8 \\[3pt]\n\t\tx^2 &= -4\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = \\pm \\sqrt{-4}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-4} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{4\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x = \\pm 2 \\textrm{i}.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-t2786\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\">\n    \n               \n                <div class=\"tutorial\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Introduction</span></div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"t2786\">?</div>\n                    </div>                    \n    \n                    <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>When solving an equation, we sometimes require taking the square root of a negative number. In such cases, we will not end up with real solutions, but imaginary solutions.</p>\n<p>To demonstrate, let's solve the equation <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"11.81ex\" height=\"2.676ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.505ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -934.9 5084.9 1152.1\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">2x^2 +8 